  <Placemark>
   <name>Gale Warning issued November 7 at 1:32AM PST until November 8 at 4:00AM PST by NWS Medford OR</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_moderate</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, south winds 15 to 25 kt
and steep seas 12 to 17 ft at 16 seconds. For the Gale
Warning, southwest winds 25 to 35 kt with gusts up to 45 kt
and very steep seas 12 to 17 ft at 13 seconds expected. For
the Hazardous Seas Watch, very steep and hazardous seas 19 to
23 ft at 16 seconds likely.

* WHERE...For the Small Craft Advisory, all areas until Saturday
afternoon when it becomes more confined to inner waters due to
a Gale Warning elsewhere. For the Gale Warning, nearly all of
the outer waters north of Cape Blanco. For the Hazardous Seas
Watch, all areas.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, until 4 AM PST Sunday.
For the Gale Warning, from 1 PM Saturday to 4 AM PST Sunday.
For the Hazardous Seas Watch, from late Saturday night through
Sunday evening.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds and very steep seas could capsize or
damage vessels. Low visibility conditions are expected.

* View the hazard area in detail at https://go.usa.gov/x6hks</Snippet>
