   <styleUrl>#sev_moderate</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the Hazardous Seas Warning, very steep and hazardous
seas 15 to 17 ft at 14 seconds and southeast winds 15 to 25 kt
with gusts up to 30 kt. For the Storm Warning, seas 16 to 21 ft
at 13 seconds and south winds 25 to 35 kt with gusts up to 50
kt expected.

* WHERE...Coastal waters from Cape Falcon to Cape Foulweather OR
out 10 NM and Waters from Cape Falcon to Cape Foulweather OR
from 10 to 60 NM.

* WHEN...Hazardous Seas Warning, until 10 AM PST Saturday. Storm
Warning, from 10 AM Saturday to 4 AM PST Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Very strong winds will cause hazardous seas which
could capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Winds are most likely to peak between 1600
and 2000.</Snippet>
