   <name>Flood Warning issued November 6 at 9:23PM MST until November 7 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by upstream dam release continues.

* WHERE...Maricopa County in south central Arizona...

* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MST Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Salt River is occurring. Recreation on or
near the Salt River will be unsafe.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 920 PM MST, an upstream floodgate release at Bartlett Dam is
causing flooding in the warned area. A streamflow gauge on the
Verde River near the Salt River confluence measured a flow around
2130 cfs.
- Flooding is occurring along the Salt River.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Mainly recreational areas along the river around and downstream
of the Verde and Salt River confluence.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
