   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...

St Johns River Near Deland affecting Volusia and Lake Counties.

.Heavy rainfall has caused the St. Johns River near Deland remain
very near Minor flood stage. The river is forecast to slowly climb
through Minor flood stage this weekend and into next week.

For the St. Johns River...including Deland...Minor flooding is
forecast.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...St Johns River near Deland.

* WHEN...Until further notice.

* IMPACTS...At 4.5 feet, Water moves into yards and approaches
buildings around Hontoon Island.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 7:30 PM EST Friday the stage was 3.9 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 3.5 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage
tomorrow morning and continue rising to 4.5 feet early Wednesday
afternoon. Additional rises are possible thereafter.
- Flood stage is 4.0 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
