   <name>Flood Advisory issued November 5 at 7:52AM MST until November 7 at 8:00AM MST by NWS Albuquerque NM</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Arroyo and small stream flooding caused by excessive
rainfall is occurring.

* WHERE...North Central Socorro County in central New Mexico...

* WHEN...Until 800 AM MST Saturday.

* IMPACTS...River or stream flows are elevated.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 751 AM MST, emergency management reported flooding in the
advisory area from rising river levels along the Rio Puerco. This
will cause arroyo and small stream flooding. Rapid river rises
will cause minor flooding in the advisory area.
- For Rio Puerco at Bernardo:
At 7:00am the stage was 15.07 feet.
Flood Stage is 19.5 feet.
Forecast: A crest of 16.9 feet is expected at 11:00pm Thursday.
- For Rio Grande at San Acacia:
At 6:45am the stage was 15.51 feet.
Flood Stage is 23.0 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
